    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classostk_1_1mathematics_1_1curvefitting_1_1interpolator_1_1_quintic_spline" kindref="compound">QuinticSpline</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A quintic spline is a piecewise fifth-degree polynomial fitted so that it passes through the given data points. The resulting interpolant is C4 continuous, and reproduces quintic polynomials exactly. It is the highest order of the spline interpolators, and is the natural choice when a smooth second derivative is needed.</para>
<para>The first and second derivatives at the two end points are estimated from the data.</para>
<para>Nodes may be uniformly or arbitrarily spaced. Uniformly spaced nodes are interpolated with a cardinal B-spline, which finds the containing interval in constant time rather than searching for it, and is therefore faster to evaluate. Which of the two is used is decided from the data and is not otherwise observable.</para>
<para>Use when the data is smooth and only values are known, but smooth higher derivatives are needed, for instance acceleration from positions. Higher order amplifies noise, so prefer clean data.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1mathematics_1_1object_1a7353155bb00668655919bf5698f74c84" kindref="member">VectorXd</ref><sp/>x<sp/>=<sp/>{{0.0,<sp/>1.0,<sp/>2.0,<sp/>3.0,<sp/>4.0,<sp/>5.0,<sp/>6.0,<sp/>7.0}};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1mathematics_1_1object_1a7353155bb00668655919bf5698f74c84" kindref="member">VectorXd</ref><sp/>y<sp/>=<sp/>{{2.0,<sp/>0.0,<sp/>6.0,<sp/>56.0,<sp/>210.0,<sp/>552.0,<sp/>1190.0,<sp/>2256.0}};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classostk_1_1mathematics_1_1curvefitting_1_1interpolator_1_1_quintic_spline_1ae573940d59f48cb5553f591413fa31dd" kindref="member">QuinticSpline</ref><sp/>interpolator(x,<sp/>y);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>value<sp/>=<sp/>interpolator.evaluate(1.5);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><ulink url="https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_87_0/libs/math/doc/html/math_toolkit/cardinal_quintic_b.html">https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_87_0/libs/math/doc/html/math_toolkit/cardinal_quintic_b.html</ulink> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
